title: "Temporal Equivalence Principle: Synchronization Holonomy in Pulsar Scintillation"
abstract: >
  This work reports a detection of non-zero synchronization holonomy in pulsar scintillation closure delays, consistent with predictions of the two-metric Temporal Equivalence Principle (TEP) framework. The primary detection from PSR J0437-4715 exhibits 13.30σ orbital modulation in Stokes-aligned signed geometric delays, directly demonstrating that the holonomy varies with the pulsar's orbital kinematics. Standard scintillation theory assumes an additive scalar path-delay model where closure residuals vanish identically; the TEP framework generalizes this by allowing environment-dependent proper time accumulation, resulting in non-zero holonomy.
version: "v0.1 (Sintra)"
